# clasp — `.clasp.json` is per-user (holds your scriptId) and `.clasprc.json`
# is the auth token. Both stay out of the repo; the user runs `clasp clone`
# or `clasp create` once locally to generate them.
.clasp.json
apps-script/.clasp.json
.clasprc.json

# QA-sim run artifacts. Each invocation of `tsx tools/qa-sim/run.ts ...`
# writes per-scenario JSON + a REPORT.md under a timestamped dir. Don't
# commit those — they're disposable R&D outputs. `baseline/` is the
# exception: when an operator promotes a snapshot (cp -r runs/<ts>
# runs/baseline), it lives in git so the diff section in subsequent
# REPORT.md is reproducible across machines.
tools/qa-sim/runs/*
!tools/qa-sim/runs/baseline/
